# {{ projectName }} architecture

Typer parses documented argument types and calls application functions. Pydantic
Settings validates application configuration when a command explicitly requests it.

## 🧭 Ownership

`cli.py` owns commands and safe terminal errors. `settings.py` owns configuration
types and source priority. Add domain scenarios and external adapters only when
needed; do not resolve FastAPI Depends outside HTTP or add a command framework.

## 🔒 Boundaries

No settings, files, connections or downloads occur during import, help or version.
The config command reads only its selected file and prints nonsecret demonstration
settings. Future secret fields require an explicit safe projection; do not print
ValidationError input or enable traceback locals. No business writes are supplied.
